anRicha LLC","url":"https:\/\/www.veganricha.com\/","logo":{"@type":"ImageObject","inLanguage":"en-US","@id":"https:\/\/www.veganricha.com\/#\/schema\/logo\/image\/","url":"https:\/\/veganricha.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/09\/cropped-cropped-veganricha-logo.png","contentUrl":"https:\/\/veganricha.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2021\/09\/cropped-cropped-veganricha-logo.png","width":96,"height":96,"caption":"VeganRicha LLC"},"image":{"@id":"https:\/\/www.veganricha.com\/#\/schema\/logo\/image\/"},"sameAs":["https:\/\/www.facebook.com\/VeganRicha","https:\/\/x.com\/veganricha","https:\/\/instagram.com\/veganricha\/","https:\/\/www.pinterest.com\/veganricha","https:\/\/youtube.com\/veganricharecipes"]},{"@type":"Person","@id":"https:\/\/www.veganricha.com\/#\/schema\/person\/008994495d9faab5cd94cbec4069b445","name":"Richa","image":{"@type":"ImageObject","inLanguage":"en-US","@id":"https:\/\/secure.gravatar.com\/avatar\/517f2e68abf7632b27af8bafc9c52286649f86d9d1c25ee8936e2387fa8c2332?s=96&d=mm&r=g","url":"https:\/\/secure.gravatar.com\/avatar\/517f2e68abf7632b27af8bafc9c52286649f86d9d1c25ee8936e2387fa8c2332?s=96&d=mm&r=g","contentUrl":"https:\/\/secure.gravatar.com\/avatar\/517f2e68abf7632b27af8bafc9c52286649f86d9d1c25ee8936e2387fa8c2332?s=96&d=mm&r=g","caption":"Richa"},"description":"Hi, I'm Richa! I create flavorful plant based recipes that are inspired by my Indian upbringing, including many gluten-free, soy-free, and oil-free options.","sameAs":["https:\/\/www.veganricha.com\/about-contact\/","https:\/\/x.com\/veganricha"],"url":"https:\/\/www.veganricha.com\/about-contact\/"},{"@type":"Question","@id":"https:\/\/www.veganricha.com\/spicy-peanut-butter-ramen\/#faq-question-1678713319645","position":1,"url":"https:\/\/www.veganricha.com\/spicy-peanut-butter-ramen\/#faq-question-1678713319645","name":"Can I make this peanut-free?","answerCount":1,"acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"To make this recipe without peanuts, you can use sunflower butter or almond butter instead of peanut butter. ","inLanguage":"en-US"},"inLanguage":"en-US"},{"@type":"Question","@id":"https:\/\/www.veganricha.com\/spicy-peanut-butter-ramen\/#faq-question-1680713725033","position":2,"url":"https:\/\/www.veganricha.com\/spicy-peanut-butter-ramen\/#faq-question-1680713725033","name":"What is gochujang?","answerCount":1,"acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Gochujang is a spicy-sweet Korean chili paste made from fermented glutenous rice and soybeans with red chilis and salt.","inLanguage":"en-US"},"inLanguage":"en-US"},{"@type":"Question","@id":"https:\/\/www.veganricha.com\/spicy-peanut-butter-ramen\/#faq-question-1680936947887","position":3,"url":"https:\/\/www.veganricha.com\/spicy-peanut-butter-ramen\/#faq-question-1680936947887","name":"Can I make this gluten-free?","answerCount":1,"acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Use Glutenfree noodles, use tamari instead of soy sauce. ensure that Gochujang is gluten-free ","inLanguage":"en-US"},"inLanguage":"en-US"},{"@type":"Question","@id":"https:\/\/www.veganricha.com\/spicy-peanut-butter-ramen\/#faq-question-1680936996950","position":4,"url":"https:\/\/www.veganricha.com\/spicy-peanut-butter-ramen\/#faq-question-1680936996950","name":"Can I make this soy-free?","answerCount":1,"acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Use chickpea tofu instead of tofu, coconut aminos for the soy sauce.  Gochujang often has soy, so use 2 teaspoons each of gochugaru pepper flakes, chickpea miso, coconut aminos and. 1 teaspoon maple syrup to make your own Gochujang. ","inLanguage":"en-US"},"inLanguage":"en-US"},{"@type":"Recipe","name":"Spicy Peanut Butter Ramen","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Vegan Richa"},"description":"Spicy peanut butter ramen is an absolute comfort food recipe with a delicious, creamy broth, gochujang flavors, lots of ginger and garlic, topped with Gochujang tofu. It&#039;s a 30-minute, One-pan meal. The noodles are cooked directly in the broth, so you only need one pot.","datePublished":"2023-04-08T04:05:00+00:00","image":["https:\/\/www.veganricha.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/04\/Peanut-Gochujang-Ramen-7928.jpg","https:\/\/www.veganricha.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/04\/Peanut-Gochujang-Ramen-7928-500x500.jpg","https:\/\/www.veganricha.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/04\/Peanut-Gochujang-Ramen-7928-500x375.jpg","https:\/\/www.veganricha.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/04\/Peanut-Gochujang-Ramen-7928-480x270.jpg"],"video":{"name":"PEANUT GOCHUJANG RAMEN | Vegan Richa Recipes","description":"PEANUT GOCHUJANG RAMEN\n\n🔸Get the WRITTEN RECIPE here - https:\/\/www.veganricha.com\/spicy-peanut-butter-ramen\/\n\n🔸SUBSCRIBE HERE: https:\/\/www.youtube.com\/veganricharecipes?sub_confirmation=1\n\n🔸My New Instant pot cookbook: https:\/\/www.amazon.com\/Vegan-Richas-Instant-PotTM-Cookbook\/dp\/0306875039\/\n\nSpicy Gochujang peanut butter ramen is an absolute comfort food recipe with a delicious, creamy broth, gochujang flavors, lots of ginger and garlic, topped with Gochujang tofu. It’s a 30-minute, One-pan meal! \n\nFor this spicy peanut butter ramen, you cook the noodles directly in the broth, so you only need one pot. I topped it with some crispy tofu, and you can use the same pot to crisp up the tofu that you use to cook the ramen. You can bake the tofu, though, if you prefer.\n\nThe peanut butter gives this ramen a creamy, rich broth, and gochujang brings sweet heat and gives this vegan ramen recipe such a special flavor! You will want to make this every day! Change up the veggies and toppings for variation.\n\n******MORE RAMEN RECIPES FROM THE BLOG******\n\nHOT AND SOUR SOUP WITH RAMEN: https:\/\/www.veganricha.com\/vegan-hot-and-sour-soup-with-ramen\/\n\nCURRY RAMEN WITH MISO LENTILS: https:\/\/www.veganricha.com\/curry-ramen-miso-lentils\/\n\nONE POT PEANUT SAUCE NOODLES: https:\/\/www.veganricha.com\/1-pot-peanut-sauce-noodles\/\n\nCOOKBOOKS BY RICHA HINGLE (VEGAN RICHA): https:\/\/www.veganricha.com\/mybooks\/\n\nConnect with me on Social Media:\n\nFACEBOOK: https:\/\/www.facebook.com\/VeganRicha\n\nINSTAGRAM: https:\/\/instagram.com\/veganricha\n\nPINTEREST: https:\/\/www.pinterest.com\/veganricha\/\n\nTWITTER: https:\/\/twitter.com\/veganricha\n\nMusic: Epidemic Sound \n\n#veganramen #gochujang #easyveganmeals  #easyveganrecipes","uploadDate":"2023-05-14T16:00:22+00:00","duration":"PT1M56S","thumbnailUrl":"https:\/\/i.ytimg.com\/vi\/OsD_7lGoynU\/hqdefault.jpg","embedUrl":"https:\/\/www.youtube.com\/embed\/OsD_7lGoynU?feature=oembed","contentUrl":"https:\/\/www.youtube.com\/watch?v=OsD_7lGoynU","@type":"VideoObject"},"recipeYield":["3"],"prepTime":"PT10M","cookTime":"PT20M","totalTime":"PT30M","recipeIngredient":["10 oz firm or extra firm tofu (pressed for at least 15 minutes and sliced into rectangles or cubes or whatever shape you like)","2 teaspoons soy sauce (or tamari )","2 teaspoons gochujang","1\/2 teaspoon garlic powder","1 teaspoon sesame oil","1 tablespoon cornstarch or tapioca starch","1 teaspoon oil (optional)","6 oz sliced mushrooms (such as white or cremini or portabella )","2 tablespoon ginger-garlic paste","3 tablespoons smooth peanut butter","1 tablespoon gochujang (or other Asian chile sauce )","1 tablespoon maple syrup","2 tablespoons soy sauce (or tamari )","4-6 cups  water or stock  (**)","6 oz ramen or thin udon noodles","lime wedges, green onions, sesame seeds"],"recipeInstructions":[{"@type":"HowToSection","name":"Make the gochujang garlic tofu.","itemListElement":[{"@type":"HowToStep","text":"Press and cube the tofu if you haven’t already and add it to a bowl.","name":"Press and cube the tofu if you haven’t already and add it to a bowl.","url":"https:\/\/www.veganricha.com\/spicy-peanut-butter-ramen\/#wprm-recipe-50571-step-0-0"},{"@type":"HowToStep","text":"In a small bowl mix the soy sauce, gochujang, garlic powder, and sesame oil and pour it over the tofu. Toss well to coat. Add 2 teaspoons of the cornstarch and toss well. If the mixture is still somewhat wet then add the rest of the cornstarch and toss well.","name":"In a small bowl mix the soy sauce, gochujang, garlic powder, and sesame oil and pour it over the tofu. Toss well to coat. Add 2 teaspoons of the cornstarch and toss well. If the mixture is still somewhat wet then add the rest of the cornstarch and toss well.","url":"https:\/\/www.veganricha.com\/spicy-peanut-butter-ramen\/#wprm-recipe-50571-step-0-1"},{"@type":"HowToStep","text":"Then either bake the tofu:  transfer the tofu cubes to a parchment-lined baking sheet and bake it at 400ºF (205c) for 20-25 minutes , or transfer them to a hot wok with a teaspoon of oil and cook them until they are crisp on most of the edges, about 5-6 minutes.","name":"Then either bake the tofu:  transfer the tofu cubes to a parchment-lined baking sheet and bake it at 400ºF (205c) for 20-25 minutes , or transfer them to a hot wok with a teaspoon of oil and cook them until they are crisp on most of the edges, about 5-6 minutes.","url":"https:\/\/www.veganricha.com\/spicy-peanut-butter-ramen\/#wprm-recipe-50571-step-0-2"}]},{"@type":"HowToSection","name":"Make the ramen:","itemListElement":[{"@type":"HowToStep","text":"I use the same wok for making the tofu as well as the ramen. Remove the tofu once crisp from the pot and then make the ramen. Add oil, mushrooms, and a good pinch of salt and cook for 2-3 minutes to brown the mushrooms on some of the edges. Then add the ginger-garlic paste, peanut butter, gochujang, maple syrup and soy sauce and mix really well. Add 1\/4 cup of the water or broth and mix in. Mix well to incorporate the peanut butter.","name":"I use the same wok for making the tofu as well as the ramen. Remove the tofu once crisp from the pot and then make the ramen. Add oil, mushrooms, and a good pinch of salt and cook for 2-3 minutes to brown the mushrooms on some of the edges. Then add the ginger-garlic paste, peanut butter, gochujang, maple syrup and soy sauce and mix really well. Add 1\/4 cup of the water or broth and mix in. Mix well to incorporate the peanut butter.","url":"https:\/\/www.veganricha.com\/spicy-peanut-butter-ramen\/#wprm-recipe-50571-step-1-0"},{"@type":"HowToStep","text":"Bring the mixture to a boil then gradually add the rest of the broth. Mix and Bring  to a good rolling boil, then add your noodles. Press to submerge in the boiling broth, then cook them according to the time on the packaging. Ramen noodles will cook pretty quickly, within 3-4 minutes, while udon noodles will take around 7-8 minutes.","name":"Bring the mixture to a boil then gradually add the rest of the broth. Mix and Bring  to a good rolling boil, then add your noodles. Press to submerge in the boiling broth, then cook them according to the time on the packaging. Ramen noodles will cook pretty quickly, within 3-4 minutes, while udon noodles will take around 7-8 minutes.","url":"https:\/\/www.veganricha.com\/spicy-peanut-butter-ramen\/#wprm-recipe-50571-step-1-1"},{"@type":"HowToStep","text":"Once the noodles are cooked to your preference, switch off the heat. Taste and adjust salt and flavor. If you want it sweeter then you can add more maple syrup. You can more salt if needed or some black pepper for extra heat.","name":"Once the noodles are cooked to your preference, switch off the heat. Taste and adjust salt and flavor. If you want it sweeter then you can add more maple syrup. You can more salt if needed or some black pepper for extra heat.","url":"https:\/\/www.veganricha.com\/spicy-peanut-butter-ramen\/#wprm-recipe-50571-step-1-2"},{"@type":"HowToStep","text":"To serve, ladle the broth into your serving bowls. Then transfer some of the noodles with mushrooms to your serving bowls. Top it with the crispy tofu, a squeeze of lime or lemon, lime wedge, green onions, and sesame seeds, and serve.","name":"To serve, ladle the broth into your serving bowls. Then transfer some of the noodles with mushrooms to your serving bowls. Top it with the crispy tofu, a squeeze of lime or lemon, lime wedge, green onions, and sesame seeds, and serve.","url":"https:\/\/www.veganricha.com\/spicy-peanut-butter-ramen\/#wprm-recipe-50571-step-1-3"},{"@type":"HowToStep","text":"To make ahead: cook the noodles separately and store. Crisp up the tofu and store. Add only 3 cups broth and boil and refrigerate after cooling. To serve, bring the broth to a boil, add noodles and serve. Refrigerate for up 3 days.","name":"To make ahead: cook the noodles separately and store. Crisp up the tofu and store. Add only 3 cups broth and boil and refrigerate after cooling. To serve, bring the broth to a boil, add noodles and serve. Refrigerate for up 3 days.","url":"https:\/\/www.veganricha.com\/spicy-peanut-butter-ramen\/#wprm-recipe-50571-step-1-4"}]}],"aggregateRating":{"@type":"AggregateRating","ratingValue":"5","ratingCount":"154","reviewCount":"10"},"review":[{"@type":"Review","reviewRating":{"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":"5"},"reviewBody":"Amazing! Have made again and again. Top rated!","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Courtney"},"datePublished":"2026-07-18"},{"@type":"Review","reviewRating":{"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":"5"},"reviewBody":"My boyfriend and I have made this recipe nearly a dozen times! We double the tofu and experiment with different crunchy toppings like sliced snap peas, julienne carrots, pickled ginger, scallions, those crunchy onions that go on green bean casserole, peanuts, etc. Our favorite variation involves fresh oyster mushrooms (which we also double) from the farmers market. I’m vegetarian so we’ll sometimes make a soft boiled egg if we want to be fancy. A showstopper recipe to impress.","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Vanessa L"},"datePublished":"2026-05-30"},{"@type":"Review","reviewRating":{"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":"5"},"reviewBody":"We make this often.  Everyone who has eaten this has loved it.  We bake the tofu and always add extra veg, what ever is on hand, bok choi, broccoli, bell peppers, carrots or snow peas all work very well.  The broth is amazing.  This meal is so satisfying, easy and delicious.","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Steve May"},"datePublished":"2026-05-07"},{"@type":"Review","reviewRating":{"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":"5"},"reviewBody":"Made this a few times - outstanding and so easy.","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Ed"},"datePublished":"2026-05-07"},{"@type":"Review","reviewRating":{"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":"5"},"reviewBody":"This was really yummy! I added some snow peas and carrots. It was a perfect weeknight meal. Thanks for the recipe.","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Carie"},"datePublished":"2026-04-24"},{"@type":"Review","reviewRating":{"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":"5"},"reviewBody":"This was a last minute, throw together something before I call for a pizza. This is faster than pizza and has so much more flavor.\r\n\r\nI did not have tofu so I tossed in edamame instead. I will definitely keep on hand just for this recipe. I also added cilantro at the end.\r\n\r\nI was so surprised that the sesame seeds at the end was so noticeable.  \r\n\r\nThe whole dish was so flavorful and a pleasure to put together at the last minute. Will be making a spot on the weekly meal rotation.","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Cathy"},"datePublished":"2026-03-24"},{"@type":"Review","reviewRating":{"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":"5"},"reviewBody":"Wow!! This is amazing!! Spicy, sweet, umami. It took all I could do to not eat the whole pot!","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Dana"},"datePublished":"2026-03-24"},{"@type":"Review","reviewRating":{"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":"5"},"reviewBody":"Yummy!!","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Meg Schultz"},"datePublished":"2026-03-15"},{"@type":"Review","reviewRating":{"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":"5"},"reviewBody":"Banging recipe! I've made it two or three times now and everyone who's tried it loved it! A friend said it's the best noodles he ever tasted, and loved the tofu too, something he'd never had before! I can't wait to make it again!","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Yann B"},"datePublished":"2026-02-15"},{"@type":"Review","reviewRating":{"@type":"Rating","ratingValue":"5"},"reviewBody":"I've made this many times, without the peanut butter. SO good!!","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Naomi"},"datePublished":"2026-01-24"}],"recipeCategory":["dinner","Main","Main Course","Soup"],"recipeCuisine":["Asian fusion"],"keywords":"peanut gochujang ramen, spicy peanut butter ramen","nutrition":{"@type":"NutritionInformation","calories":"440 kcal","carbohydrateContent":"63 g","proteinContent":"21 g","fatContent":"13 g","saturatedFatContent":"2 g","sodiumContent":"683 mg","fiberContent":"5 g","sugarContent":"8 g","unsaturatedFatContent":"10 g","servingSize":"1 serving"},"@id":"https:\/\/www.veganricha.com\/spicy-peanut-butter-ramen\/#recipe","isPartOf":{"@id":"https:\/\/www.veganricha.com\/spicy-peanut-butter-ramen\/#article"},"mainEntityOfPage":"https:\/\/www.veganricha.com\/spicy-peanut-butter-ramen\/"}]}</script>
