	<li id="comment-777915" class="comment even thread-odd thread-alt depth-1 parent">
		<article id="div-comment-777915" class="comment-body">
			<footer class="comment-meta">
				<div class="comment-author vcard">
										<b class="fn">Vanessa L</b> <span class="says">says:</span>				</div><!-- .comment-author -->

				<div class="comment-metadata">
					<time datetime="2026-05-30T18:21:25-07:00">May 30, 2026 at 6:21 pm</time>				</div><!-- .comment-metadata -->

							</footer><!-- .comment-meta -->

			<div class="comment-content">
				<p><img class="wprm-comment-rating" src="data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODdhAQABAPAAAP///wAAACwAAAAAAQABAEACAkQBADs=" data-lazy-src="https://www.veganricha.com/wp-content/plugins/wp-recipe-maker/assets/icons/rating/stars-alt-5.svg" alt="5 stars" width="80" height="16" /><br />
My boyfriend and I have made this recipe nearly a dozen times! We double the tofu and experiment with different crunchy toppings like sliced snap peas, julienne carrots, pickled ginger, scallions, those crunchy onions that go on green bean casserole, peanuts, etc. Our favorite variation involves fresh oyster mushrooms (which we also double) from the farmers market. I’m vegetarian so we’ll sometimes make a soft boiled egg if we want to be fancy. A showstopper recipe to impress.</p>
			</div><!-- .comment-content -->

			<div class="reply"><a rel="nofollow" class="comment-reply-link" href="#comment-777915" data-commentid="777915" data-postid="50519" data-belowelement="div-comment-777915" data-respondelement="respond" data-replyto="Reply to Vanessa L" aria-label="Reply to Vanessa L">Reply</a></div>		</article><!-- .comment-body -->
	<ol class="children">
